he "Islamic State" terror group.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz calls for unity at CSU party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d15659b1a04c9e9347f6abc30ec0ecbe2026dee7ae3e5690d06f37e4832caec9</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-unity-at-csu-party-conference/live-79749353--718b2e6284ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-unity-at-csu-party-conference/live-79749353?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With his coalition under pressure, Merz delivered an address at the close of the CSU conference in Munich. Meanwhile, fire has largely destroyed Hitler's former Eagle's Nest retreat. DW has more</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hitler's Eagle's Nest retreat catches fire, police say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aea67fa45d8355da2be2b06ecbab2b839913975d25ce82dd2c6556dfed6698ed</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T02:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat-catches-fire-police-say/a-79747820--4006d6d04b27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat-catches-fire-police-say/a-79747820?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities have arrested a suspect as firemen try to put out the fire in Bavaria, near the Austrian border.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Wadephul says 'threat of famine' due to ongoing wars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:367353f7ff5566fe613ac4c544bba8f64106c0a48fdb04f6c44995d2f6c96f51</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-wadephul-says-threat-of-famine-due-to-ongoing-wars/live-79738902--60ffe6da3f19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-wadephul-says-threat-of-famine-due-to-ongoing-wars/live-79738902?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul is joining counterparts in Turkey for discussions on a range of interlinked geopolitical crises. Back in Germany, the Bavarian CSU party begins its two-day conference in Munich.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany revive its economy before the AfD gains ground?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:177cfd3f6546ebcbaf8bd947dca32420e4fa53c7cc6b56a3a6662a8dd7177b16</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102--1f6301348482.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Can new growth sectors create jobs and ease voters' economic fears, thereby helping contain the far-right AfD?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b573047688d97b5334856eb5221750e88209c5d60a50d957bba14a83320c1ef0</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane is the clear front-runner for football's most prestigious individual prize, which will be awarded on Monday. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Football: German coach Hürzeler flying high in Premier League</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fa4e5076b8a25f5135c4aada46a537e37d7c527766bd35a4b39f63255c53d9a</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-h_rzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763--701507a044eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-hürzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fabian Hürzeler is younger than his star player, a fellow Premier League German. But, contrary to his reputation in his homeland, Hürzeler has become a popular figure both on and off the pitch in England.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1c4a17104858ee9be801111eec1c5da027abd9daf4fc2dfb72f9d6edb16e75a</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
